Perf lab mutation for jobs 07 to 12 (LTO, -O2, PGO series). Base: freeunit master 856d23b9e.
Adds -O2 after the -O line of auto/cc/test, in the gcc and the clang branch. The last -O wins.
The explicit -fno-strict-aliasing and -fno-strict-overflow stay in force: gcc does not let -O2 switch off a flag the user set.
tools/perf-lab/remote.sh applies this with patch -p1 to the unpacked tree, before ./configure.
diff --git a/auto/cc/test b/auto/cc/test
index ac4d5f3..ad5b4d4 100644
--- a/auto/cc/test
+++ b/auto/cc/test
@@ -72,6 +72,7 @@ case $NXT_CC_NAME in
         NXT_CFLAGS="$NXT_CFLAGS -std=gnu11"
 
         NXT_CFLAGS="$NXT_CFLAGS -O"
+        NXT_CFLAGS="$NXT_CFLAGS -O2"
         NXT_CFLAGS="$NXT_CFLAGS -Wall -Wextra"
 
         #NXT_CFLAGS="$NXT_CFLAGS -Wunused-result"
@@ -116,6 +117,7 @@ case $NXT_CC_NAME in
         NXT_CFLAGS="$NXT_CFLAGS -std=gnu11"
 
         NXT_CFLAGS="$NXT_CFLAGS -O"
+        NXT_CFLAGS="$NXT_CFLAGS -O2"
         NXT_CFLAGS="$NXT_CFLAGS -Wall -Wextra"
 
         #NXT_CFLAGS="$NXT_CFLAGS -Wunused-result"
